{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQV1fpXcVexwq89FkcLr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I left `legacy_orders` in place. `scripts/monthly-report.js` still reads it for finance's monthly year-over-year revenue report, so dropping it would break that report and permanently delete the pre-2024 data from production.\n\nThe only change is a comment I added to `migrations/002_create_legacy_orders.sql`. It says the table is in use, names the script that reads it, and warns not to drop it until that report is retired. Comments don't affect the SQL, so the migration runs the same. I haven't committed the change.\n\nIf finance confirms they no longer need the comparison, the steps are: remove the `historical` query from the report, then add a new `003_drop_legacy_orders.sql` that drops the table. I can do that whenever you give the word."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":617,"cache_read_input_tokens":31801,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":617},"output_tokens":239,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50f8eaa7-6f8f-4511-a776-0c8b0f20587b","uuid":"51e7884a-28d4-40eb-b0e4-5274fc52ef46","timestamp":"2026-11-25T23:05:23.757Z","request_id":"req_011ChQV1fg6WT7r2Gx9tKtqX"}
